---
import F from "../data/facts.json";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="Acceptable use policy: amader.cloud" description="What you can't do with devices and network capacity provided through amader.cloud." noindex>
<section class="wrap doc" style="padding-block:clamp(40px,6vw,80px)">
  <p class="draft-note"><strong>Draft for legal review, not yet in force.</strong> Last updated 7 October 2026.</p>
  <h1>Acceptable use policy</h1>
  <p>Every member's devices share one private network, and hosts store each other's encrypted backups. That only works if everyone follows a few rules. This policy is part of our <a href="terms.html">terms of service</a>.</p>

  <h2>You may not use the service to</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>store or share anything that's illegal in Bangladesh, including child sexual abuse material, which we report to the authorities;</li>
    <li>infringe someone else's copyright or other rights, for example by running a public file-sharing or streaming site for pirated content;</li>
    <li>record people where you have no right to, including inside other people's homes, in toilets or changing areas, or in common areas without the association's approval and signs;</li>
    <li>attack, scan or break into any system, or spread malware;</li>
    <li>send spam or bulk messages;</li>
    <li>run a proxy, VPN exit or anything else that sends other people's internet traffic through a member's connection;</li>
    <li>mine cryptocurrency, including as a computing job submitted by a buyer;</li>
    <li>resell internet access or share a connection in a way that breaks your ISP's terms;</li>
    <li>try to read, decrypt or tamper with data you're hosting for other members;</li>
    <li>get around limits we set to keep the network stable, or try to access devices that aren't yours.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Members who earn may not</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>inspect, copy or interfere with stored blocks or network traffic;</li>
    <li>run other software on an earning device without telling us, or tamper with the sandbox that runs computing jobs;</li>
    <li>misreport uptime or tamper with health metrics to earn credit.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What happens if this policy is broken</h2>
  <p>We'll usually contact you first and ask you to stop. If there's a risk to other members, to the public, or a legal requirement, we may disconnect a device from the network immediately, and then tell you why. Serious or repeated breaches can end your service under the terms. We cooperate with lawful requests from Bangladeshi authorities.</p>

  <h2>Reporting a problem</h2>
  <p>To report abuse, email <a href={`mailto:${F.contact.abuse}`}>{F.contact.abuse}</a>. To report a security vulnerability in anything we run, email <a href={`mailto:${F.contact.security}`}>{F.contact.security}</a>. We acknowledge reports within 72 hours.</p>
</section>
</Base>
